WEBVTT

01:15.950 --> 01:17.160
Jimmy K.

01:18.620 --> 01:20.413
Yeah, go for Jimmy K.

01:20.497 --> 01:22.414
Tell your division we're going silent,
Isaac's orders.

01:22.499 --> 01:24.167
-Call your boats back. Radio silent.
-Pull it out!

01:24.250 --> 01:25.668
I swear to God,
if you don't do it, I will.

01:25.752 --> 01:28.505
-I said maybe.
-Alright, copy.

01:28.588 --> 01:30.840
-This is gonna hurt.
-It already fucking hurts!

01:36.387 --> 01:38.640
Jesse, don't let me...

01:39.182 --> 01:40.600
You can't let me die.

01:40.683 --> 01:42.352
-Yeah, I know.
-No, you don't.

01:42.435 --> 01:44.020
Listen, if I pull it,
it's gonna tear an artery.

01:44.104 --> 01:45.814
-I need to push it through.
-How do you know that?

01:45.896 --> 01:47.774
-What if it's the wrong way?
-I know where the arteries are.

01:47.857 --> 01:49.609
-No, you don't, you're not a doctor!
-Dina, shut up!

01:54.572 --> 01:55.824
Hey.

01:55.907 --> 01:56.908
Dina.

01:58.785 --> 02:00.703
I got you, alright?

02:00.787 --> 02:01.996
I got you.

02:09.753 --> 02:12.632
I know, I know.
I know. Have some, okay?

02:12.715 --> 02:14.175
-No.
-It's gonna help. Have some.

02:14.259 --> 02:15.593
I said no.

02:23.268 --> 02:24.269
Okay.

02:27.188 --> 02:28.189
Just do it.

02:52.463 --> 02:53.590
It's me.

02:54.966 --> 02:56.009
Jesse! Dina!

02:56.091 --> 02:57.677
What's the name of your horse?

02:57.760 --> 02:59.971
Shimmer. I'm alone.
Open the fucking door!

03:10.773 --> 03:12.734
-Where is she?
-What happened to you?

03:13.902 --> 03:16.279
Dina? Is she--

03:16.362 --> 03:17.906
She's okay.
She's in the dressing room.

03:17.989 --> 03:20.658
-Dressing room.
-Ellie, where were you?

04:17.839 --> 04:18.966
Hi.

04:22.470 --> 04:23.721
Let me see.

04:45.743 --> 04:47.578
Is the baby...?

04:49.497 --> 04:51.541
-It's okay.
-How do you know?

04:52.792 --> 04:54.294
I just do.

05:12.061 --> 05:13.187
Sit over there.

05:14.188 --> 05:15.189
Alright.

05:23.573 --> 05:24.574
Shirt off.

05:33.666 --> 05:35.710
Okay, arms up.

05:36.544 --> 05:38.379
Three, two, one.

06:08.117 --> 06:09.952
So, are you gonna tell me what happened?

06:14.374 --> 06:15.583
I found her.

06:17.251 --> 06:18.628
I found Nora.

06:20.963 --> 06:21.964
Good.

06:23.633 --> 06:24.967
Does she know where Abby is?

06:25.510 --> 06:28.513
Yes, but she only said two words.

06:29.680 --> 06:31.641
"Whale," and then "wheel."

06:33.183 --> 06:36.354
-What does that mean?
-I don't know. Maybe nothing.

06:37.146 --> 06:39.148
She was infected,
it was already setting in.

06:55.373 --> 06:57.082
I made her talk.

07:02.171 --> 07:04.632
I thought it would be harder to do.

07:06.509 --> 07:08.386
But it wasn't.

07:09.846 --> 07:11.431
It was easy.

07:13.641 --> 07:15.726
I just kept hurting her.

07:21.941 --> 07:23.276
Did you kill her?

07:24.193 --> 07:25.194
No.

07:26.487 --> 07:27.697
I left her.

07:30.908 --> 07:33.661
Yeah, well, maybe she got
what she deserved.

07:39.250 --> 07:40.835
Maybe she didn't.

08:13.242 --> 08:14.994
It was a long time ago.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.207
Before I came to Jackson.

08:23.294 --> 08:25.963
There was a Firefly base
in Salt Lake City.

08:26.756 --> 08:28.299
They had a hospital there.

08:28.382 --> 08:30.676
They were gonna use me to make a cure.

08:33.011 --> 08:34.889
But it meant that I would have died.

08:36.807 --> 08:39.727
And Joel found out.

08:46.776 --> 08:49.987
And he killed everyone in the hospital.

08:51.989 --> 08:53.491
Everyone.

08:55.743 --> 08:57.870
He killed Abby's father.

09:00.206 --> 09:03.918
He was a doctor,
and Joel shot him in the head.

09:06.087 --> 09:07.588
To save me.

09:15.096 --> 09:17.056
So, that's why they came.

09:23.062 --> 09:24.647
Did you know who they were?

09:32.780 --> 09:34.574
But I knew what he did.

09:40.538 --> 09:41.998
I'm sorry.

09:51.882 --> 09:53.467
We need to go home.

10:48.898 --> 10:50.650
Do you have any extra nine-millimeter?

10:55.655 --> 10:56.781
Thanks.

11:11.379 --> 11:13.547
You shouldn't be on your feet yet.

11:13.631 --> 11:15.216
I'll go back to the couch in a second.

11:16.258 --> 11:17.551
I promise.

11:20.137 --> 11:21.138
Give me your wrist.

11:25.393 --> 11:27.061
The other one.

11:44.912 --> 11:46.205
It's for good luck.

11:47.415 --> 11:49.417
Not sure it's been working for you.

11:50.334 --> 11:51.627
I'm alive.

11:53.212 --> 11:55.548
I can do this alone,
if you want Ellie to stay.

11:55.631 --> 11:56.799
No.

12:01.137 --> 12:02.638
We'll be safer together.

12:03.556 --> 12:05.099
Our rendezvous point's not far.

12:05.683 --> 12:07.727
Assuming Tommy's there, we should be back

12:07.810 --> 12:10.146
-well before sundown.
-Okay, good.

12:11.313 --> 12:13.315
You okay to barricade?

12:13.399 --> 12:15.526
Yeah. Go.

12:15.609 --> 12:16.610
Yeah.

12:53.189 --> 12:55.733
-Where's the rendezvous?
-The bookstore.

13:00.029 --> 13:01.781
You ever gonna tell me
how you found the theater?

13:03.032 --> 13:05.284
You ever gonna tell me
what happened to you last night?

13:09.205 --> 13:11.332
We followed the likeliest path
into the city.

13:11.415 --> 13:13.459
Found the place you stashed Shimmer.

13:13.542 --> 13:16.086
She's still there doing alright.
Not that you asked.

13:16.170 --> 13:18.756
And then, we saw the WLF sign
on the TV station,

13:18.839 --> 13:21.550
figured that's where you went,
split up a two-square-mile area

13:21.634 --> 13:23.135
around it and began searching.

13:23.219 --> 13:24.845
That's how I found the theater.

13:26.055 --> 13:27.515
Oh, you make it sound easy.

13:28.557 --> 13:31.977
It took two days and a lot of close calls.

13:35.272 --> 13:36.398
Thank you.

13:37.691 --> 13:39.235
I mean it, honestly.

13:41.070 --> 13:42.488
Look, I know you're angry--

13:42.571 --> 13:44.698
Last night, Dina said, "I can't die."

13:44.782 --> 13:47.993
Not, "I don't want to die." "I can't."

13:48.077 --> 13:49.912
And then I offered her whiskey,
and she refused.

13:50.788 --> 13:54.124
Dina, the girl who's never turned down
a free drink in her life,

13:54.208 --> 13:56.293
seconds before
I was gonna push a crossbow bolt

13:56.377 --> 13:57.920
-through her leg.
-That's weird.

13:58.003 --> 14:00.005
-I don't know why she--
-Yes, you do.

14:00.089 --> 14:02.341
I'm not stupid and I'm not blind.

14:02.424 --> 14:04.635
Ellie, I see the way
you two look at each other.

14:05.344 --> 14:06.804
It's different now.

14:08.097 --> 14:11.725
Yeah, and I bet she even tells you things
she wouldn't tell me.

14:11.809 --> 14:13.227
Like how she's pregnant.

14:16.522 --> 14:17.606
Fuck.

14:21.235 --> 14:22.987
Oh, shit, you were guessing?

14:24.029 --> 14:25.072
Oh, God.

14:29.034 --> 14:31.787
Look, she's obviously gonna tell you.

14:31.871 --> 14:35.249
So, just act surprised, okay?

14:35.332 --> 14:37.459
None of this has to
change things between us.

14:37.543 --> 14:39.712
Everything changing
doesn't have to change things?

14:40.754 --> 14:43.048
Well, how 'bout this for something new?

14:43.132 --> 14:46.635
I'm gonna be a father,
which means I can't die.

14:46.719 --> 14:48.762
But because of you,
we're stuck in a war zone.

14:49.430 --> 14:50.848
So, how 'bout we skip the apologies

14:50.931 --> 14:53.267
and just go find Tommy
so I can get us and my kid

14:53.350 --> 14:54.560
the fuck outta Seattle?

15:17.249 --> 15:19.001
There's more than one of her?

15:19.084 --> 15:20.961
I guess so. I don't know.

15:22.838 --> 15:24.632
We need to move faster.

15:43.734 --> 15:45.277
Please tell me we're close.

15:46.487 --> 15:48.030
Think we have two more blocks.

15:49.365 --> 15:52.326
Let's give it a minute,
see if it dies down, and then we'll--

15:53.619 --> 15:54.745
-Shit.
-Go.

15:54.828 --> 15:56.580
-I see him!
-You're fucking dead, Scar!

15:57.289 --> 15:59.875
-Nowhere to run!
-There, there, there. Go! Get down!

15:59.959 --> 16:02.086
He's heading off in the garage.
Keep going!

16:03.671 --> 16:05.339
Get on the ground!

16:05.422 --> 16:06.590
You piece of shit!

16:08.008 --> 16:10.761
The world is not in balance,
but I've done my part to right it.

16:10.844 --> 16:12.262
How'd you get past our line?

16:13.514 --> 16:14.723
How?!

16:14.807 --> 16:17.810
The world is not in balance.
But I have done my part to right it.

16:17.893 --> 16:20.479
She has led me through the storm.
Now I must rest.

16:20.562 --> 16:21.772
-May she guide me.
-I'm sorry, what?

16:21.855 --> 16:22.856
May she guide me.
May she guide me.

16:24.066 --> 16:25.734
Get his clothes off.

16:25.818 --> 16:26.902
No! No!

16:27.736 --> 16:30.656
Wait! Wait! No!
Stop it! Get off of me!

16:31.323 --> 16:33.325
-Stop!
-Come on, you little piece of shit!

16:33.409 --> 16:34.868
-Drag him.
-Fucking go!

16:34.952 --> 16:36.996
-Let's go!
-Let's fucking go!

16:39.248 --> 16:41.290
Let's go! Go!

16:47.006 --> 16:49.383
-Get the fuck off!
-Ellie.

16:50.426 --> 16:51.427
Ellie.

16:52.928 --> 16:54.346
-Ellie!
-What?!

16:54.430 --> 16:56.015
There are six of them and two of us.

16:56.098 --> 16:57.975
-What do you think would've happened?
-He's a fucking kid!

16:58.058 --> 17:00.352
Ellie, these people
are shooting each other,

17:00.436 --> 17:02.563
lynching each other,
ripping each other's guts out.

17:02.646 --> 17:03.814
Even the kids.

17:04.481 --> 17:06.483
I am not dying out here.

17:07.526 --> 17:09.528
Not for any of them.

17:09.611 --> 17:12.321
This is not our war.

17:17.243 --> 17:18.369
Let's go.

17:31.800 --> 17:34.178
Can't leave it there.
You gotta move your truck.

17:44.021 --> 17:45.898
Good news.

17:45.981 --> 17:48.817
Melissa and Kristi are saying
the storm's a convergence zone.

17:52.946 --> 17:54.323
It's gonna get even bigger.

17:56.325 --> 17:59.203
Orders have been relayed verbally,
everything's set.

18:04.124 --> 18:05.876
All the officers are on board,

18:05.959 --> 18:08.378
but I think the rank and file
are a little scared.

18:08.462 --> 18:10.089
Aren't you?

18:12.549 --> 18:15.719
It'll be dark by 21:30.

18:15.803 --> 18:17.971
-We'll start the staggered load in--
-Any word on Abby?

18:20.891 --> 18:22.768
Not since yesterday.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.729
And we still haven't found Owen.

18:29.149 --> 18:30.567
Mel is missing now, too.

18:31.985 --> 18:36.406
So, her entire crew just disappears,
tonight of all nights?

18:39.785 --> 18:41.120
We still have Manny.

18:41.203 --> 18:43.038
Well, we have a lot of Mannys, don't we?

18:43.122 --> 18:44.957
And enough Owens and Mels.

18:46.083 --> 18:47.668
But only one Abby.

18:50.587 --> 18:52.005
Okay, what the fuck?

18:52.589 --> 18:54.550
She's a good soldier. Great, even.

18:54.633 --> 18:56.677
But we have an entire
fuckin' army out there

18:56.760 --> 18:58.554
and you're acting like
she's the most important.

18:59.596 --> 19:00.681
What--

19:01.682 --> 19:03.016
You in love with her or something?

19:05.435 --> 19:09.273
I mean, I don't know.
You wouldn't be the first old man to--

19:09.356 --> 19:11.567
Okay, okay. No.

19:27.207 --> 19:31.336
By the time the sun comes up tomorrow,
there's a very good chance you'll be dead.

19:32.921 --> 19:34.965
There's an even better chance
I'll be dead.

19:36.592 --> 19:39.428
So then, what happens to that
entire fucking army out there,

19:39.511 --> 19:42.181
who despite their badass name,
are very much sheep?

19:43.849 --> 19:45.267
Who leads them?

19:46.560 --> 19:48.020
Who secures our future?

19:50.522 --> 19:52.191
It was supposed to be her.

20:00.157 --> 20:01.992
Well, she's fucked off, Isaac.

20:05.120 --> 20:06.371
So, maybe it wasn't.

20:27.559 --> 20:28.644
Fuck.

20:30.437 --> 20:31.730
Is that your shit?

20:32.189 --> 20:33.440
Yeah.

20:33.523 --> 20:35.400
Alright. So, if he's not here...

20:35.484 --> 20:37.361
It's gonna be fine.
He'll make it back.

20:37.444 --> 20:40.072
-Well, what if he's in trouble?
-"What if"?

20:40.155 --> 20:42.324
He is in trouble.
We're all in trouble.

20:45.953 --> 20:49.748
Here we are again.
You and me in bad fuckin' weather.

21:29.037 --> 21:30.455
You picked a good one.

21:31.832 --> 21:33.375
I should have thought of that.

21:37.087 --> 21:40.424
Listen, about me and her,
I don't really know what to say.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.013
Right now, we got a lot of problems.

21:46.596 --> 21:48.307
Like a wounded pregnant girl.

21:48.390 --> 21:50.475
Maybe Tommy's dead.
Maybe we'll be dead.

21:50.559 --> 21:54.187
So, let me at least
just get this one off the table.

21:56.648 --> 21:58.442
Yes, I love her.

22:00.235 --> 22:01.737
But not the way you do.

22:11.163 --> 22:13.457
Remember that group
that stopped by Jackson

22:13.540 --> 22:15.792
for a few weeks
on their way south to Mexico?

22:16.877 --> 22:20.964
From Alberta?
Yeah, they had some decent shit to trade.

22:21.048 --> 22:23.342
There was this girl with them.

22:23.425 --> 22:24.926
She was a couple years older than me.

22:25.010 --> 22:27.846
I don't know if you remember.
She was selling paintings,

22:27.929 --> 22:29.806
like landscapes and shit.

22:29.890 --> 22:32.309
-Were they good?
-No.

22:33.643 --> 22:35.312
I bought four of 'em.

22:38.732 --> 22:40.442
That fuckin' feeling,

22:41.485 --> 22:45.030
when you're falling for someone
and they're falling right back.

22:51.161 --> 22:54.414
-So, what happened?
-Best two weeks of my life.

22:55.040 --> 22:56.875
But she couldn't stay.

22:56.958 --> 22:59.044
Didn't want to abandon
her family like that.

23:00.170 --> 23:02.506
So, she asked me to go with them instead.

23:04.716 --> 23:06.051
And I wanted to.

23:07.636 --> 23:08.929
More than anything.

23:10.180 --> 23:11.765
Then, why didn't you?

23:14.309 --> 23:18.355
Because the people of Jackson
took me in, raised me, cared for me,

23:18.438 --> 23:21.942
because everyone there
is counting on me to be the next Maria.

23:23.735 --> 23:27.864
Because I was taught
to put other people first.

23:30.283 --> 23:32.327
Okay.

23:33.328 --> 23:38.834
Got it. So, you're Saint Jesse of Wyoming
and everyone else is a fucking asshole.

23:38.917 --> 23:42.629
You can make fun of me all you want,
but let me ask you this, Ellie.

23:42.712 --> 23:46.091
I go with that girl to Mexico,
who saves your ass in Seattle?

23:48.885 --> 23:50.303
Under fire! I repeat!

23:50.387 --> 23:53.598
We are under fire.
Under fire, Southlake Marina.

23:53.682 --> 23:55.684
Sniper, not a Scar!

23:55.767 --> 23:58.562
Unidentified-- Goddammit!

23:58.645 --> 24:00.522
Two of us pinned down. We need backup!

24:00.605 --> 24:02.190
-No radios. Repeat.
-Sniper.

24:02.274 --> 24:03.733
-No radios.
-It's gotta be Tommy.

24:06.445 --> 24:08.363
This is South Lake.
There's two piers right here.

24:09.281 --> 24:10.449
It's gotta be one of them.

24:10.532 --> 24:12.325
Alright, pack your shit.
We're going up.

24:45.108 --> 24:46.234
You hear that?

24:47.110 --> 24:48.361
It's in the right direction.

24:49.988 --> 24:52.991
I don't see an easy way north,
but if he got there,

24:53.074 --> 24:54.576
it means we can, too.

24:55.660 --> 24:56.995
Ellie.

24:57.078 --> 24:58.371
The wheel.

24:58.455 --> 25:00.207
-The whale.
-What?

25:00.290 --> 25:02.209
-She's in the fucking aquarium.
-Who?

25:02.292 --> 25:04.711
Abby, the one who killed Joel.
She's in the aquarium.

25:04.794 --> 25:06.087
It's too far to swim. We need a boat.

25:06.171 --> 25:08.465
-What are you talking about?
-What?

25:08.548 --> 25:10.759
No, Tommy's over there.
That's where we're going.

25:15.180 --> 25:16.890
You don't know that's him.

25:17.933 --> 25:19.434
-Yes, we do.
-We don't.

25:19.518 --> 25:21.353
And even if it is,
he's got them pinned down.

25:21.436 --> 25:22.979
For now. They called for backup.

25:23.063 --> 25:25.232
Then, he'll pin more of them down.
I know him.

25:25.315 --> 25:27.859
He would want me to do this.

25:27.943 --> 25:30.362
And Jesus Christ,
if three more people had voted with you,

25:30.445 --> 25:31.655
you'd be coming with me.

25:36.701 --> 25:37.702
I voted no.

25:41.998 --> 25:43.375
Why?

25:43.458 --> 25:46.044
Because everything you do, you do for you.

25:46.127 --> 25:47.921
Oh, my God.

25:48.004 --> 25:49.548
-Ellie.
-Oh, my God.

25:49.631 --> 25:52.259
Ellie, it wasn't in the best interest
of the community.

25:52.342 --> 25:54.261
Fuck the community!

25:54.344 --> 25:56.429
All you do is talk about
the fucking community.

25:56.513 --> 25:57.639
You hypocrite.

25:57.722 --> 25:59.516
You think you're good and I'm bad?

26:00.809 --> 26:03.436
You let a kid die today, Jesse.

26:03.520 --> 26:06.314
Because why? He wasn't in your community?

26:07.774 --> 26:09.526
Let me tell you about my community.

26:10.902 --> 26:13.446
My community was beaten to death
in front of me

26:13.530 --> 26:15.615
while I was forced to fucking watch.

26:15.699 --> 26:17.993
So, don't look at me
like you're better than me

26:18.076 --> 26:19.411
or like you'd do anything differently

26:19.494 --> 26:23.039
if you were in my shoes,
because you're not, and you wouldn't.

26:29.796 --> 26:31.339
I really hope you make it.

27:38.531 --> 27:39.949
Hey, let's move, come on.

27:40.784 --> 27:42.077
Come on, we gotta meet 'em out there.

28:21.282 --> 28:22.367
Load 'em up.

28:23.576 --> 28:24.577
Let's go!

28:31.418 --> 28:32.961
Last one's on board.

32:06.257 --> 32:09.719
No! I'm not from here! I'm not a Wolf!

32:10.219 --> 32:11.429
Tell them.

32:40.750 --> 32:43.044
The village. The village!

32:45.922 --> 32:46.923
Leave her!

37:21.614 --> 37:25.534
...for her, so don't make me sound like
I'm being some kind of heartless bitch.

37:25.618 --> 37:29.664
I'm not. And let's be honest,
this isn't about them anyways, Owen.

37:29.747 --> 37:33.042
You're talking about being behind
enemy lines alone at night.

37:33.125 --> 37:34.835
This is suicide
under normal circumstances

37:34.919 --> 37:36.420
and you want to do this now?

37:36.504 --> 37:38.047
Do you even understand what's going on?

37:38.130 --> 37:40.883
I understand everything,
but I don't have a choice, do I?

37:40.967 --> 37:42.760
It's Abby.

37:42.843 --> 37:45.638
Of course, you have a choice.
And so do I.

37:45.721 --> 37:48.474
And I am choosing no,
also because it's Abby.

37:48.557 --> 37:50.601
Fine, I'll do it on my own, like always.

37:50.685 --> 37:52.311
I can make it there and back in 30.

37:52.395 --> 37:53.729
If you're still here, you can get on board

37:53.813 --> 37:55.982
and keep going with us.
If you're not, you're not.

37:57.108 --> 37:59.151
Fuck you, Owen.

37:59.235 --> 38:00.403
Hands up.

38:04.740 --> 38:07.618
-Where's Abby?
-You gotta be kidding me.

38:07.702 --> 38:09.453
Okay. Easy.

38:13.749 --> 38:15.543
I'm the one who kept you alive, right?

38:22.174 --> 38:23.634
We don't know where she is.

38:23.718 --> 38:26.595
You were just talking about her,
so, yes, you fucking do.

38:32.184 --> 38:33.561
You, bring me that map.

38:34.478 --> 38:37.023
You're gonna point to where Abby is,

38:37.106 --> 38:40.568
and then you're gonna do it,
and it better fucking match.

38:45.781 --> 38:47.450
You have five seconds.

38:48.951 --> 38:51.037
-Four.
-She's gonna kill us either way.

38:51.120 --> 38:52.204
No, I won't.

38:53.914 --> 38:55.624
Because I'm not like you.

38:57.668 --> 38:58.669
Three.

39:01.714 --> 39:02.715
Two.

39:04.133 --> 39:06.719
I'll do it. I'll do it.

39:07.928 --> 39:09.096
I'll show you.

39:10.973 --> 39:12.308
Slowly.

39:14.060 --> 39:15.269
Slowly.

39:34.705 --> 39:36.040
Oh, God.

39:42.797 --> 39:44.340
Oh, God.

39:48.636 --> 39:51.305
Knife? Do you have a knife?

39:53.349 --> 39:55.434
I have, like, 30 seconds.
Get the fuck over here, please.

39:55.518 --> 39:57.478
Please, please, please.

39:59.772 --> 40:02.316
Knife. Knife.

40:02.400 --> 40:05.861
You're gonna take it out.
You're gonna get it out.

40:06.779 --> 40:07.780
What?

40:09.907 --> 40:12.284
-I don't know how to do that.
-I do. I do.

40:12.993 --> 40:15.121
One incision. That's all it is.

40:15.204 --> 40:17.456
And then, be sure to tie the cord.

40:18.916 --> 40:21.168
Work fast. Work fast.

40:22.461 --> 40:24.004
Work fast.

40:24.088 --> 40:26.465
-Work fast. Very fast.
-Okay. Okay.

40:30.302 --> 40:31.512
How deep?

40:31.595 --> 40:33.889
-Deeper than you think.
-Which way?

40:35.599 --> 40:36.684
Which way?

40:39.103 --> 40:41.605
Low transverse. Transverse.

40:41.689 --> 40:44.150
What? I don't know what that means.

40:44.233 --> 40:45.526
Low transverse.

40:46.777 --> 40:48.487
Low transverse.

40:48.571 --> 40:51.615
What? Tell me what that means.

40:53.367 --> 40:55.786
You're doing good.
You're doing really good.

40:59.206 --> 41:00.374
Is it out?

41:03.377 --> 41:04.587
Is it out?

42:01.060 --> 42:02.061
Ellie?

42:04.855 --> 42:05.856
Ellie.

42:08.776 --> 42:10.027
Oh, God.

42:12.238 --> 42:13.239
Hey.

42:19.537 --> 42:21.330
Let's go, come on. It's okay, it's okay.

42:22.081 --> 42:24.291
Come on. Come on.

42:40.140 --> 42:41.141
Shit.

42:45.104 --> 42:46.438
Oh, thank God.

43:12.756 --> 43:14.216
The park is no go,

43:14.300 --> 43:16.635
so we stick to the south
on our way outta town.

43:17.886 --> 43:20.222
Not a good idea
to move her in this weather

43:20.306 --> 43:22.266
so pray for sunshine.

43:22.349 --> 43:24.268
Get the horses at first light
and don't look back.

43:42.578 --> 43:43.871
Hey.

43:45.414 --> 43:48.000
You know, they were part of it, too.

43:50.377 --> 43:51.879
They made their choices.

43:52.630 --> 43:54.048
That's all there is to it.

44:00.554 --> 44:02.264
But Abby gets to live.

44:03.766 --> 44:04.892
Yeah.

44:05.643 --> 44:07.811
Are you able to make your peace with that?

44:09.605 --> 44:11.190
Guess I'll have to.

44:24.536 --> 44:26.288
I'm gonna start packin' the duffels.

44:42.513 --> 44:44.264
Thank you for coming back.

44:47.059 --> 44:49.144
Maybe I didn't want to.

44:50.604 --> 44:52.189
Maybe Tommy made me.

44:53.607 --> 44:54.692
Did he?

45:01.865 --> 45:02.991
Nope.

45:07.871 --> 45:09.832
Because you're a good person.

45:13.711 --> 45:14.753
Yeah.

45:17.339 --> 45:19.341
But also, the thought did occur,

45:20.634 --> 45:24.430
if I were out there somewhere,
lost and in trouble,

45:26.557 --> 45:28.851
you would set the world
on fire to save me.

45:32.479 --> 45:33.856
I would.

45:56.754 --> 45:57.880
Stand up.

45:59.798 --> 46:01.467
Stand up!

46:01.550 --> 46:03.343
Hands in the air or I shoot this one too.

46:03.427 --> 46:04.887
-Just run, Ellie!
-Shut the fuck up!

46:04.970 --> 46:06.555
Stop! Stop!

46:18.650 --> 46:19.985
You.

46:20.068 --> 46:21.945
Just let him go.

46:24.698 --> 46:25.991
He killed my friends.

46:26.074 --> 46:27.951
No, I did.

46:28.035 --> 46:30.496
I was looking for you.
I didn't mean to hurt them.

46:32.831 --> 46:36.084
I know why you killed Joel.
He did what he did to save me.

46:36.168 --> 46:37.878
I'm the one that you want.

46:39.922 --> 46:41.548
Just let him go.

46:43.509 --> 46:45.219
I let you live.

46:47.679 --> 46:49.598
I let you live.

46:52.100 --> 46:53.727
-And you wasted it.
-No, no, no!

47:10.077 --> 47:11.078
Hey.

47:11.161 --> 47:12.996
-Oh, shit.
-You up?

47:13.080 --> 47:15.082
-Well, yeah, now.
-Cool. Alright, come on.

47:15.165 --> 47:16.625
Isaac wants to talk to us.

47:18.168 --> 47:20.879
Okay. Just let me wake up.

47:20.963 --> 47:23.006
-I'll be there in five minutes.
-Alright.

47:23.090 --> 47:24.842
It's your funeral if you make him wait.

47:24.925 --> 47:26.134
Uh-huh.
